// =====================================================================
// /app/briefs/create-brief-quick — New brief · Vibe Code block.
//
// The whole create flow. Three routes, and the two questions that
// decide whether the AI writes something specific or something that
// could belong to anyone:
//
//   [AI]      answer the questions, and the brief is written before it
//             opens. One OpenRouter call, the section model, not the
//             legacy JSON body.
//   [Guided]  same questions, no writing. The brief opens in the
//             builder with the answers saved, so every per-section
//             Write-with-AI already has the product and the channel.
//   [Blank]   name it and go.
//
// The questions exist because the model cannot be specific about a
// product it was never given. "No product, this is brand or organic
// content" is a real answer and is recorded as such, so nothing is
// invented to fill the gap.
//
// Product picker: choose from the workspace catalog, or paste a URL
// and Firecrawl reads the page once. Adding writes the product to the
// account, so the catalog builds itself as briefs get made.
//
// The brief is created WITH its project linked, taken from the project
// page that opened this modal. Vibe Code CAN map a linked record on
// create; the old comment claiming otherwise is what kept the
// unassigned workaround alive. The project id is read once in an
// inline useState initialiser, because URL parsing anywhere else stops
// Softr's analyzer registering the create action.
//
// SOFTR CONFIG:
//   1. Rendered as the /new-brief modal, opened from a project page
//      so the URL carries ?recordId=<projectId>.
//   2. Sources: briefs, accounts, products, Firecrawl, OpenRouter.
//      MULTI-SOURCE, so every hook passes `from`.
//   3. Visibility: logged-in users.
// =====================================================================

import { useMemo, useState } from "react";
import {
  datasource, useRecords, useRecordCreate, useProxyFetch, q,
